page('2. Text-as-data method and validation')
add('The estimand is the presence of a <b>reported claim</b>: a suspect or accused person attempted or completed seizure of an officer firearm, immediately followed by police shooting that person in West Bengal. Fatal and nonfatal outcomes must be coded separately. Earlier weapon theft, weapons supplied by an accomplice, police victims and confiscated illegal arms are distinct categories.')
table([['Retrieval route','Definition','Unique records'],['A: broad geography and violence','WB desk/URL or place-name proxy, plus shooting/encounter words or police-and-death words','3,271'],['B: weapon taking, all locations','Gun/weapon terms plus snatch/grab/wrest/seize/disarm/overpower stems','977'],['C: encounters, all locations','Encounter/gunfight/shootout/crossfire plus police, suspect or death terms','3,154'],['Union of A, B, C','Overlapping routes deduplicated by archive/publication-date field plus normalized headline','7,356']],[133,310,73])
add('Normalization uses Unicode NFKC, lowercasing, punctuation-to-space and whitespace collapse. Full regular expressions, original text and candidate source-line references are saved. Broad words deliberately overretrieve: for example, police seizure of illegal arms is not suspect seizure of a police gun. Date-headline deduplication can merge distinct same-title items or retain one article listed on different dates; only case review can create an event roster.')
table([['Independent subagent review','Result','Interpretation'],['All 52 WB-proxy route-B records','49 other; 3 unresolved; 0 explicit full target sequence','Only four literally use snatch; no historical zero-event inference'],['206 broader primary focus headlines','16 flagged for body review','Screening of relevant wording, not a completed body census'],['Simple random sample of 100 WB-proxy negatives','0 visible missed shooting/encounter headlines; 1 ambiguous violence headline','Seed 20261027; frame 125,579 unique primary records outside route A']],[160,175,181])
add('The negative audit checks headline-visible retrieval misses only. It cannot estimate how often article bodies contain an omitted mechanism. No precision/recall estimate for the full target event is claimed. Separate model passes are useful checks, but do not substitute for independent human coding, adjudication or measured intercoder agreement. This follows the problem-specific validation emphasis of Grimmer and Stewart. [6]')
