page('3. Calculating the 5.26% benchmark')
add('Assume exactly three event times independently drawn uniformly over a fixed interval of T days. Order them t1 &lt; t2 &lt; t3. There is no pair within 24 hours precisely when t2 - t1 &gt; 1 and t3 - t2 &gt; 1. Subtract the required gaps, producing t1, t2 - 1 and t3 - 2. The ordered configurations now occupy a simplex with side T - 2, rather than T. Three-dimensional volume scales with the cube of that side.')
add('<b>P(any pair within 24 hours | N=3, T) = 1 - ((T - 2)/T)<super>3</super></b>')
add('At T=112: 1 - (110/112)<super>3</super> = 0.05262049 = <b>5.262%</b>. This includes any of the three possible pairs, not just the named October pair. For calendar dates, all three dates differ with probability (T-1)(T-2)/T<super>2</super>. Its complement is the shared-date probability.')
table([['Illustrative window ending 27 October','Days','Any shared date','Any pair within 24h'],*[[x['start'],x['calendar_days'],pct(x['p_any_same_calendar_day_given_exactly_3'],3),pct(x['p_any_pair_within_24h_given_exactly_3_continuous'],3)] for x in probs['conditional_three_event_windows']]],[220,55,115,126])
add('<b>Window selection matters.</b> July 8 was chosen because an event occurred then; October 27 was noticed because of the cluster. These are not independently chosen testing boundaries. Exactly three must also be the complete event count. The table does not correct every search across dates, states, narratives or window lengths. The continuous 112-day calculation treats the selected calendar window as a 112-day interval; actual timestamps are uncertain.')
head('An alternative: assume a baseline rate')
add('Under an independent constant-rate Poisson process, let m = r/365, where r is the assumed annual number of reported events of this exact type. P(two or more on a specified day) = 1 - exp(-m)(1+m). This is a different question from noticing a close pair afterward. [13]')
table([['Assumed events/year','2+ on specified day','Any 2+ date in a year','Next event within 24h'],*[[x['assumed_events_per_year'],pct(x['p_two_or_more_specified_day'],5),pct(x['p_any_calendar_day_two_or_more_in_365_days'],2),pct(x['p_next_event_within_24h'],2)] for x in probs['poisson_sensitivity'] if x['assumed_events_per_year']<=20]],[115,135,133,133])
add('These rates are assumptions, not fitted estimates from the headline corpus. Do not infer that a low probability of clustering under this model implies an equally high probability of fabricated accounts.',True)

