head('A comparable measure for the requested question')
add('Build a common event-level dataset across every state and period. Within uniformly retrieved police-shooting reports, record G = immediate gun-taking claims, N = reviewed nonmatches, and U = unresolved mechanisms. With D = G + N + U, report the narrative-share bounds <b>[G/D, (G+U)/D]</b>. Report fatal and nonfatal shares separately. This makes missing mechanisms explicit.')
add('Code the state government on the incident date, including coalition status and transition dates. Compare equal observation periods and consistent press coverage. For frequency of genuine attempts, use prisoner transports/reconstructions or armed-custody exposure as the denominator. Population alone is an imperfect substitute. A party-effect analysis needs all states, pretrends, state and time controls, and credible treatment-timing assumptions; a short selected list cannot establish causation.')
add('Do not divide the three 2026 externally verified events by historical headline totals, or compare three article-body matches against zero historical headline matches as an incidence change. The units, time coverage and detection procedures differ.',True)

page('5. Alternative explanations and research decisions')
table([['Explanation/model','How it could generate clustering','Evidence that would help distinguish it'],['Independent rare events','Unrelated incidents occasionally occur close together','Complete event roster and independently specified baseline/window'],['Shared operational exposure','More reconstructions or transports on particular dates raise opportunities','Daily reconstruction/transport counts, escort assignments, restraint and firearm-retention records'],['Common unsafe practice or changed operations','Teams share procedures or face a common operational change','SOPs and dated instructions; consistent before/after records across districts'],['Shared account or reporting process','Standard police language, wire duplication or attention can repeat narratives','Separate contemporaneous statements, unique article IDs, independent witnesses; entity/event deduplication'],['Staged or unlawful shootings','A purported seizure could be used to justify a shooting','Independent forensic and inquiry findings, scene video, weapon custody, ballistic and medical evidence']],[115,190,211])
add('These are competing possibilities, not probabilities assigned to the incidents. The timing data alone cannot rank them. A Bayesian probability for accurate accounts versus staging requires explicit priors and the likelihood of the evidence under each hypothesis, neither supplied by the headline corpus.')
add('Even modest dependence changes the timing benchmark. At a fixed mean of ten events/year, the chance of at least two on a specified day is 0.03685% under Poisson, 0.07111% under an illustrative gamma-Poisson model with shape 1, and 0.29323% with shape 0.1. The latter models allow daily intensity variation. Their parameters are illustrative, not estimated.')
head('What has and has not been established')
add('Established: the local folder and source coverage; a reproducible historical search; an auditable set of candidate records and exclusions; three distinct 2026 reported fatal encounters invoking the mechanism; and independently checked timing calculations. Not established: a complete historical count of the mechanism, its true incidence, an empirical probability that both October accounts are accurate, or a causal party effect.')
